# Line-ending policy for the program.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   CI's second run failed on windows-latest only:
#       ConfigurationError: rule integrity check failed: endpoint.json
#   Sentinel Blue's rule manifest stores a SHA-256 over the RAW BYTES of each rule
#   file. Git's automatic LF->CRLF translation on Windows checkout changes those
#   bytes, so the integrity check fails on every Windows clone. Local runs and the
#   Linux runner both passed; the defect was invisible until a cross-platform run.
#
#   Content-addressed files must never be line-ending translated.

# Normalise text in the repository, check out LF everywhere. Deterministic across
# platforms, which is what every hash, signature, and canonicalisation here assumes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary-safe: these are hashed byte-for-byte by rule_manifest.json.
# -text disables ALL translation, so the checked-out bytes equal the committed bytes.
blue-team/rules/*.json     -text
blue-team/config/*.json    -text
blue-team/schemas/*.json   -text

# Fixture and evidence material that is signed or digested over raw bytes.
exercise/config/*.json     -text
exercise/white/*.json      -text
exercise/evidence/*.json   -text

# Shell scripts and hooks must keep LF or they will not execute.
*.sh                       text eol=lf
00-shared/tools/hooks/*    text eol=lf
